  /* ── D189: the turn-rate view of a stick, for the app ─────────────────
     The same law the Core inverts (zs_mouse.c zs_mouse_model_stick /
     zs_mouse_model_frac), on a RESOLVED model (mouseTranslation.
     resolvedAimModel): a stick magnitude s past the dead zone is u =
     (s - dz) / (1 - dz) of the travel, the game's curve makes that a share
     of full turn, and the turn rates (vx across, vy up) make it deg/s. The
     app uses it to SHOW deg/s and to keep a deg/s Smart Action step's stick
     fallback near the same turn; the Core does its own inverse every tick.
     The dead zone is read as a circle here (a square one differs only on a
     diagonal, and only for what the app displays). */
